Let \(\mathfrak g\) be a finite-dimensional simple complex Lie algebra with long-root square two, \(k\in\mathbb Z_{>0}\), and \(G\) the simply connected compact group with complexified Lie algebra \(\mathfrak g\). For integrable simple modules \(L_k(\lambda),L_k(\mu)\), with dominant integral labels satisfying \((\lambda,	heta),(\mu,	heta)\le k\), the [derived collision product](#ch13-theorem-derived-fusion-of-integrable-modules) at distinct points \(p,q\) in the ambient universal-affine category, computed with degreewise finite-top Weyl resolutions, satisfies \[L_b\odot(L_k(\lambda),L_k(\mu))\cong igoplus_{
u\in P_k^+}N_{\lambda\mu}^{
u}L_k(
u)\otimes H_b(\Omega G;\mathbb C),\qquad b\ge0.\] Here \(	heta\) is the highest root, \(N_{\lambda\mu}^{
u}\) are the Verlinde multiplicities and \(P_k^+\) is the set of integrable highest weights. Multiplication into the simple-vertex-algebra fusion output is Verlinde multiplication tensored with augmentation of the loop-space factor: it retains exactly the loop-degree-zero summands, without specifying a product on all loop-homology classes.
